# Cloud Run source deploys default to .gitignore's rules when no
# .gcloudignore exists — which silently excluded data/chroma/ (the actual
# vector index) from the very first deploy, leaving the container with an
# empty database despite a "successful" build. This file exists specifically
# to override that: everything .gitignore excludes stays excluded EXCEPT the
# one directory the running app actually needs at runtime.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
venv/
.venv/
*.log
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
.git/

!data/chroma/
